From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bringup <bringup@t1100.local>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:20:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: t1100: swap the touch axes for the landscape panel

The panel is mounted in landscape while the digitizer reports in its
native portrait coordinates.  With touchscreen-inverted-x alone, taps in
the four corners of the visible area came back as (8, 64), (46, 2153),
(1560, 2163) and (1577, 43): the axes are swapped relative to the
display.

Add touchscreen-swapped-x-y (keep the X inversion: the controller
reports 1600 - x).  The same four corners now report (65, 23),
(2166, 51), (2151, 1558) and (54, 1560), i.e. the visible 2176x1600
area.  Tested on boot_touch4.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts
@@ -257,8 +257,10 @@
 		touchscreen-size-x = <1600>;
 		touchscreen-size-y = <2176>;
 		/* measured: the controller reports 1600 - x */
 		touchscreen-inverted-x;
+		/* panel used in landscape: swap the touch axes after the X inversion */
+		touchscreen-swapped-x-y;
 
 		/* VLDO28 -> GPIO163 load switch; the driver enables "vdd". */
 		vdd-supply = <&touch_avdd>;
 	};
-- 
